From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:03:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] reference-ril: Fail unknown requests in requestCallSelection

The switch's default case only asserts, so in release builds (NDEBUG)
an unexpected request fell through to at_send_command() with an
uninitialized atCommand. clang-r596125 (22) reports this as
-Werror,-Wsometimes-uninitialized. Complete the request with
RIL_E_REQUEST_NOT_SUPPORTED and return instead.

Change-Id: I72c3abb552132a87d8cb502b52a8c250226b1f75
---
 reference-ril/reference-ril.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/reference-ril/reference-ril.c b/reference-ril/reference-ril.c
index b2c4270..c82c3df 100644
--- a/reference-ril/reference-ril.c
+++ b/reference-ril/reference-ril.c
@@ -555,6 +555,8 @@ static void requestCallSelection(
             break;
         default:
             assert(0);
+            RIL_onRequestComplete(t, RIL_E_REQUEST_NOT_SUPPORTED, NULL, 0);
+            return;
     }
     at_send_command(atCommand, NULL);
     // Success or failure is ignored by the upper layer here.
